\description{
Generate a NIMBLE model for insect biomass, diversity, or both responses
with additive temporal and spatial effects. The model supports a shared
cubic cyclic spline for temporal variation and a shared latent spatial
autocorrelation process when the corresponding options are enabled.
}
\details{
The function constructs NIMBLE model code as a character string, writes
the generated code to an R script, and invisibly returns the model code
together with metadata describing the model specification and the
temporal and spatial parameters required to fit the model.

The temporal component can be specified as a linear quadratic effect or
a penalized cubic cyclic spline. For a shared cubic cyclic spline, both
responses use the same latent temporal curve. When both responses are
included, the biomass loading is fixed to one and the diversity loading
is estimated to identify the scale of the shared process.

The spatial component can be specified using coordinate-based effects or
a latent spatial autocorrelation process. When spatial autocorrelation
is shared between responses, both responses use the same latent spatial
field. If both responses are included, the biomass loading is fixed to
one and the diversity loading is estimated.

The model also supports continuous covariates as fixed effects,
categorical covariates as shared random effects, and optional random
intercepts for year, locality, and replicate. Covariate effects are shared
across biomass and diversity when both responses are fitted.

The spatiotemporal structure is additive: temporal and spatial effects
enter the response-specific linear predictors as separate terms. The
function does not generate a location-specific temporal interaction or
a dynamic spatial process.


For a cubic cyclic spline, the penalty matrix is symmetrized before
eigendecomposition. Eigenvalues below the relative threshold are
discarded, and the temporal basis is rotated into the retained
eigenbasis. The generated coefficient priors use the retained
eigenvalues to scale the coefficient precision.

For spatial autocorrelation, the covariance between spatial locations
is defined using an exponential function of the distance between them,
with a range parameter and a spatial standard deviation. The generated
model expects the spatial distance matrix and associated indexing
variables to be supplied in the NIMBLE data or constants as appropriate.

When both responses are included and a process is shared, one loading
is fixed to one to identify the scale of the latent process; the loading
for the second response is estimated. When only one response is
included, its loading is fixed to one.

The model is additive in space and time. It does not represent a
space-by-time interaction, location-specific temporal trajectories, or
a dynamic spatial process.
}
